Error: Jet.PublicDunderName: `__public_dunder_probe` is a Core machine name, which is `priv`
  --> <corelib>/Core/Collections/Set.jet:3:1
    |
  3 | __public_dunder_probe: fn() {}
    | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `__` name is Core's machine space: user source can't spell one, so only Core and the code the compiler generates reach it, and it never joins Core's public surface
 Fix: Declare it `priv __public_dunder_probe`, or give a public item a name without the leading `__`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.PublicDunderName
